<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Highland Clearances</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1750–1860</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Highland Clearances were the eviction of large numbers of tenants from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scottish-highlands">Scottish Highlands</a> and islands, mainly between about 1750 and 1860. Landowners removed them to make way for large sheep farms and later deer forests, often resettling them on small coastal crofts. Many emigrated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, and the Clearances remain a bitter memory in Scottish history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/highland-clearances.jpg" alt="Highland Clearances" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sarah Egan · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vuiamor2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
